{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "urn:emir:schema:extract:1",
  "title": "emir extract",
  "description": "GDS -> DSPF. `tool` quantus: PVS LVS and Quantus; `dry_run` true: the plan only, nothing was run (`ready` says whether --run could run it; `missing` says what is not); `dry_run` false: LVS matched and Quantus wrote `dspf`. PVS and Quantus are licensed tools: an agent asks the person before --run. `tool` magic: magic (open source) extracted the cell with every resistor's layer, width, length and place (`magic.path`: a magic with the geoout patch) and emir wrote `dspf` (also the RC netlist an rcc simulation runs, `rc_netlist`); `unchecked_layers`: magic's conductors the process file gives no limit (their current is in the IR drop); `work_dir`: where magic ran (`magic/` under `out_dir`, a directory of emir's own); `floating_capacitance`: capacitor nodes on no net of the network (EMIR-W646); `diagonal_resistors`: the DSPF's resistors on diagonal shapes, whose width is magic's tile extent (EMIR-W647; `emir run` lists them as not checked). Quantus documents also hold ready, kind, cdl, tools, settings, missing, lvs, ccl, steps; magic ones process, rc_netlist, magic, magicrc, files, ports, port_pins, nets, resistors, capacitors, devices, layers, unchecked_layers, nets_without_resistance, floating_capacitance, diagonal_resistors, guessed_terminals, out_dir.",
